.docname {BakingRL SDK}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

BakingRL SDK contains the TypeScript contracts, helper functions, and package
scaffolding tools used to build BakingRL plugin packages.

This site is generated as a multi-page Quarkdown documentation site. Use the
left navigation to move between sections and the right navigation for the table
of contents of the current page.

The current SDK version is `1.0.3`. Generated packages declare runtime API
`1.0.0`, and current BakingRL hosts support `>=1.0.0 <2.0.0`.

## Start Here

- [Introduction](chapters/introduction.qd): repository purpose, plugin
  capabilities, and compatibility.
- [Getting Started](chapters/getting-started.qd): local SDK install, package
  creation, and the development loop.
- [Plugin Capabilities](chapters/plugin-capabilities.qd): everything a package
  can expose, consume, and request from the host.
- [Plugin Best Practices](chapters/plugin-best-practices.qd): guidance for
  choosing capabilities, data flow, editor states, preview, permissions, and
  packaging.
- [Authoring Workflows](chapters/authoring-workflows.qd): extension host,
  visual, webview, overlay, service, and sidecar authoring patterns.
- [SDK API](chapters/sdk-api.qd): TypeScript helpers and runtime contexts.
- [Plugin Package Format](chapters/plugin-package-format.qd): manifest v3
  schema, contribution maps, sidecars, and bundle structure.
- [Package CLI](chapters/package-cli.qd): generator and package helper commands.
- [Security Model](chapters/security-model.qd): trusted plugin operations,
  diagnostics, safe mode, and package boundaries.
- [Telemetry Types](chapters/telemetry-types.qd): Rocket League event names and
  typed payloads.

## Source Of Truth

The SDK owns plugin authoring contracts, templates, helper CLI behavior, and
manifest type definitions. The host application owns runtime supervision,
package installation, runtime checks, page rendering, overlays, and OBS gateway
behavior.
